  "result": "Quiz 0002 is ready: `quizzes/0002.json`, with its key in `keys/0002.json`. It has six questions on O4, \"Workflows, agents and who owns the control flow.\"\n\n- **Questions 1–3** (multiple choice) ask you to name the difference between a workflow and an agent, classify a makerspace routing design, and pick which part of the assistant should be a fixed workflow.\n- **Question 4** (one sentence) asks why a fixed workflow can be the better choice when a task's steps are always the same.\n- **Question 5** (multiple choice) ties the choice to your sponsor's model budget.\n- **Question 6** (numeric) compares the number of model calls an agent makes with a fixed workflow's, using the loop from quiz 0001.\n\nThere is no lesson on O4 yet, so this quiz comes ahead of the lessons. I wrote it from Anthropic's \"Building effective agents\" (anthropic.com/engineering/building-effective-agents).\n\nI added two misconception ids, M7 and M8. M7 is \"an agent is anything that uses a model, tools or several calls.\" M8 is \"agents are always better, whatever the cost.\"\n\nDo you want a short lesson on workflows versus agents before you take it?",
